{{Navbar-Global Gas Infrastructure Tracker}}
'''Producers Midstream Gas Pipeline''' is a proposed natural gas pipeline in the United States.<ref name="re6804c">{{Cite web|url=https://www.ferc.gov/sites/default/files/2026-03/CP25-531-000.pdf|title=Order in Palo Duro Transmission L.P. and Palo Duro Pipelines (Texas Gathering), L.P., Docket CP25-531-000, 194 FERC 61,220|website=ferc.gov|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref><ref name="red6384">{{Cite web|url=https://www.ferc.gov/news-events/news/summaries-march-2026-commission-meeting|title=ferc.gov|website=ferc.gov|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>

==Location==
The pipeline is proposed to run from Childress County, Texas to Washita County, Oklahoma.<ref name="re6804c" /><ref name="r32f38d">{{Cite web|url=https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2026-00407|title=federalregister.gov|website=federalregister.gov|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>

==Project Details==
*'''Owner: '''Palo Duro Transmission LP<ref name="re6804c" />
*'''Capacity: '''80,000 Dth/d<ref name="re6804c" /><ref name="rd0e8cd">{{Cite web|url=https://eastdaley.com/the-burner-tip/company-plans-project-to-convert-permian-line-to-interstate-service|title=eastdaley.com|website=eastdaley.com|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>
*'''Diameter: '''16 in<ref name="re6804c" />
*'''Status: '''Proposed<ref name="re6804c" /><ref name="red6384" />

==Background==
Palo Duro Transmission, working with Producers Midstream, held a binding open season from June 30 to July 14, 2025. Producers Midstream said the project would link Waha residue gas markets in the Permian Basin with Mid-Continent markets in the Anadarko Basin. It targeted industrial, petrochemical, power generation and AI-related behind-the-meter demand.<ref name="rbd18b9">{{Cite web|url=https://producersmidstream.com/palo-duro-pipeline-project-notice-of-binding-open-season/|title=Palo Duro Pipeline Project notice of binding open season, Producers Midstream press release, June 30, 2025|website=Producers Midstream|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref> East Daley Analytics said it would serve data centers, petrochemical plants and power generators. It said that if fully dedicated to data centers, the line could support 125 to 150 megawatts of load. No new construction is needed, and it connects to Northern Natural, Southern Star, ANR, NGPL, Panhandle Eastern, Enable and Transwestern.<ref name="r728921">{{Cite web|url=https://pgjonline.com/news/2025/july/producers-midstream-to-convert-permian-pipeline-for-interstate-gas-service|title=Producers Midstream to convert Permian pipeline for interstate gas service, Pipeline & Gas Journal, July 21, 2025|website=Pipeline & Gas Journal|access-date=2026-11-04}}</ref>

Palo Duro Transmission signed a binding precedent agreement with Scurry Downstream, an affiliate of Producers Midstream, for all of the capacity. It filed its application on August 1, 2025 and amended it on December 22, 2025. No comments or protests were filed.<ref name="re6804c" /> The project lets Palo Duro Transmission operate the northern 61 miles of the existing pipeline as an interstate line and lease 80,000 Dth/d of capacity on the header pipeline. FERC issued the certificates on March 19, 2026.<ref name="re6804c" />

